  "worked_solution": "First, we notice that\n\n$$\n(k+2)!=(k+2)(k+1)!\n$$\n\nThen, we can cancel the $k!$ that occurs in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(k+2)((k+1)!)^{2}}{((k+2)!)^{2}} & =\\frac{(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!\\cdot (k+1)!}{(k+2)!\\cdot (k+2)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!\\cdot (k+1)!}{(k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!\\cdot (k+2)\\cdot (k+1)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(k+2)}\\cdot \\cancel{(k+1)!}\\cdot \\cancel{(k+1)!}}{(k+2)\\cdot \\cancel{(k+1)!}\\cdot \\cancel{(k+2)}\\cdot \\cancel{(k+1)!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
